 got hooked in right away just being  in that basement with  wanda and agnes  or should i say agatha and what's  interesting is they took the route  of anything like a christmas carol story  right where  agatha's now bringing wanda through the  past and now we're actually getting a  true  wanda origin story now what's smart  about this and made me excited about the  mcu doing  shows now is that we can really go into  origin stories for characters we've  known that didn't really get one  in a movie and you're also gonna get  payoff now that you can't get in a  marvel movie with super  emotional character beats and that  happens a lot in this episode  and really it every flashback counts  here of wanda i mean  just them showing that shell that came  from stark  that ended up being the reason her  parents died was crazy to actually  visually see and it hit more and i love  how they connected  that in that moment she was watching a  sitcom as like  something to attach to and protect her  and that she grew up around this and it  makes so much sense  to why she would create the sitcom world  in the show  we see so i really like that i love  also the actors who played the kids of  pietro and wanda i thought they were  great  and then we go to this other flashback  here where we see wanda actually  is confronted by the mind stone and i  love this flash we get of like  her legitly in the scarlet witch outfit  i thought that was crazy and i  really want to know more theories you  guys have about that and kind of can  explain  why she would see that vision and what  that could mean for the future for her  character i'd love to hear your thoughts  on that  but it's really interesting because  they're also kind of  delving into this confusion about the  character of  wanda or you say scarlet witch in the  mcu compared to  her being like oh is she magneto's  daughter from that version  is she a mutant but they kind of combine  it where she was a  baby witch like agatha says  and 