 getting that  character growth we need for her to  set up in the finale to be the hero we  know of wanda and to set up this  big moment where they actually say her  name is scarlet witch for the first time  in the mcu  and that she's this chaos magic and what  was really  well well well first off there's a  post-credits scene so please if you  haven't seen it it's a big one so i'm  going to talk about in a second but this  is your warning to go watch it first and  come back  but it's interesting because it's  connected to hayward right and how  we get this moment we're waiting for the  time of like okay what happened after  end game  with wanda and where did she go how did  she handle the vision thing and  we get to see it and it was haunting  just seeing visions body parts  on this table here that hayward had and  hayward planted the idea in her head  to like yeah you can bring vision back  because it's all for him it's all for  his greed and wanting  vision himself and he knew he needed  wanda there so it really is this  mastermind plan by  hayward and what you see in the  post-credits scene is that  coming to life for him and he's getting  what he wants is that  okay great i got something with wanda's  power on it i'm using it and he's  actually taking the real vision  body and bringing him back to life in  some kind of form which is the  post-credits scene which was just  crazy so we're going to see that come  out next week which i think is going to  be the big  reveal of like what's really going on  with this new version of vision  but i really loved agatha in this  episode and of course  obviously elizabeth olsen just kills it  per usual but catherine han really stood  out here she did amazing and i thought  it was so cool  seeing agatha harkness now at the end in  her full witch form  holding the kids and they had that  really just amazing makeup on her  costume design is just awesome and it's  also interesting because i do think  they're setting up  because